1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Good morning.

2
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:02,334
What’s the occasion?

3
00:00:02,335 --> 00:00:02,961
[JAO] Nothing.

4
00:00:03,002 --> 00:00:04,712
I just wanted to give you flowers.

5
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:06,423
“Smell me now, dye me later”?

6
00:00:06,464 --> 00:00:07,464
I put a lot of thought into that.

7
00:00:07,465 --> 00:00:08,675
[HAN BIN] You’re almost there, Pearl.

8
00:00:08,717 --> 00:00:09,884
You have the right words.

9
00:00:09,926 --> 00:00:12,136
You just need the confidence to say it.

10
00:00:12,137 --> 00:00:13,847
I will finish this some other time.

11
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,975
[PEARL] I just need to get ready for our celebration later.

12
00:00:17,016 --> 00:00:19,894
[PEARL] Katig’s anniversary should be fun!

13
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:21,229
[CAROL] I hope they like it.

14
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:22,856
- [HAN BIN SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Morning! - Good morning!

15
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:23,690
[HAN BIN SPEAKS SIARGAONON] Morning!

16
00:00:23,691 --> 00:00:24,815
[JAO] Happy anniversary!

17
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:25,817
You see this?

18
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:28,278
[KARA] They all have jobs because of you.

19
00:00:28,486 --> 00:00:30,071
[KARA] And you see this crazy girl?

20
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:32,699
[KARA] This crazy girl has a job that she loves

21
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,826
because of a crazy guy like you.

22
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:37,161
You guys all mean so much to me.

23
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:40,789
[CROWD CHEERING AND CHANTING]

24
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:42,083
[JAO] Wait!

25
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,418
[TANTAN] Sir Jao...

26
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:45,753
You don’t have a place to stay.

27
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:47,672
I’m all alone.

28
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:48,839
We’ll help you.

29
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:52,051
Starting today, you can call me Uncle Jao, too.

30
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:53,094
Sounds good?

31
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:54,762
- That can wait! - Good evening, sir.

32
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:55,764
[MAN] Do you have a room?

33
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:58,725
Caitlyn?

34
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:01,770
[JAO] Come on, Kara. Let’s head back out.

35
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:06,231
Caitlyn!

36
00:01:06,232 --> 00:01:08,234
- [MAN] Wait. - [JAO] Hey.

37
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:11,696
Sorry, I don’t think Kara wants to talk to you.

38
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,406
Kara?

39
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,074
Her name is Caitlyn.

40
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:17,911
The fact that you don’t even know that name…

41
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:20,538
That means this is none of your business, man.

42
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:23,415
Well, I know her enough to say that she doesn’t want to talk to you.

43
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:25,835
And who are you, exactly?

44
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:27,337
Jeremy.

45
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:29,422
Her ex-fiancé.

46
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:36,262
Look, I’m not trying to cause any trouble.

47
00:01:36,846 --> 00:01:38,848
I didn’t even know Caitlyn was here.

48
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:40,892
I just came as a tourist, man.

49
00:01:44,395 --> 00:01:45,396
[JAO] Kara?

50
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:47,315
[JAO] Kara?

51
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:58,743
[ALON BY JL]

52
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:11,690
[FIRE CRACKLING] [LOUD MUSIC IN THE BACKGROUND]

53
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:15,695
[LOUD MUSIC IN THE BACKGROUND]

54
00:03:15,737 --> 00:03:16,863
[CAROL] Hello!

55
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,031
- [HAN BIN] Hello! - Mom!

56
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:21,158
Pearlita. Hello!

57
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:22,368
Why don't you join us there?

58
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:24,287
- Dance some more! - [PEARL LAUGHS]

59
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:25,496
- [HAN BIN] No, thanks. - [CAROL] This dance.

60
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:27,956
- [PEARL LAUGHS] - [CAROL] Didn’t you want to dance?

61
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:30,460
- Or you want another… beer? - [ARIEL] Mom!

62
00:03:30,501 --> 00:03:32,670
[ARIEL] Jeremy’s here. Kara’s ex!

63
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,756
Oh! Okay, uh…

64
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:37,342
I’ll take care of it. You guys stay here.

65
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:39,385
[ARIEL] Go on. It’s her ex.

66
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:40,427
[CAROL] Is he handsome?

67
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:41,845
- [ARIEL] Go. - [CAROL] Fine. Stay here.

68
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:45,058
Oh no... Kara’s ex-boyfriend?

69
00:03:45,099 --> 00:03:47,100
- [ARIEL] Ex-fiancé! - [PEARL GASPS]

70
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:49,604
Exes belong in the past.

71
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,188
[PEARL] Even if…

72
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:53,191
You know about him already?

73
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:54,233
A little.

74
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:57,195
Caitlyn is very secretive, but…

75
00:03:57,612 --> 00:04:00,907
sometimes I hear her and our mom talking about Jeremy.

76
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:02,950
Wait, so…

77
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:05,662
Kara’s real name is Caitlyn?

78
00:04:06,162 --> 00:04:07,455
- Yeah. - Yeah!

79
00:04:07,664 --> 00:04:08,665
You didn’t know?

80
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:09,874
No.

81
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:10,917
[PEARL] What?

82
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:14,003
How can you not know, Sir Han?

83
00:04:14,045 --> 00:04:16,838
Kara always talks about that, even to our guests!

84
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:18,841
Actually, all of our guests.

85
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:21,468
How she changed her name to

86
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:26,099
Kara because “karajaw” means “awesome”.

87
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:29,936
Yeah, because her life started to become awesome when she lived here.

88
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:32,230
I mean,

89
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:33,940
I didn’t know all of this.

90
00:04:34,482 --> 00:04:36,192
When I met Kara,

91
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:38,444
she’s already Kara.

92
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:41,363
I didn’t know she has a secret identity.

93
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:44,075
Han Bin oppa, it’s not a secret identity!

94
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:46,953
It’s more like a rebranding.

95
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:49,372
[ARIEL] Yeah.

96
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:53,334
How about you, Han Bin oppa?

97
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:56,087
Do you have a secret identity?

98
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:58,631
- Me? - [ARIEL] Yeah.

99
00:05:01,592 --> 00:05:03,428
Or a…

100
00:05:03,803 --> 00:05:06,389
new rebranding that you’re not telling us?

101
00:05:08,057 --> 00:05:09,058
No!

102
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,144
I’m just Han Bin.

103
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:12,937
Han Bin oppa.

104
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:15,273
- Han Bin oppa. Sir Han. - [HAN BIN] Yes.

105
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:19,192
I think we need

106
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:21,528
hot chocolate and suman. (Sticky rice cake)

107
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:23,822
[SIARGAONON] Sounds amazing!

108
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:25,825
- Good idea! - [HAN BIN] Let’s go?

109
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:27,868
- Yes, Ariel will help you! - Yes! I will!

110
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:28,994
- Yeah, let’s get... - Let’s go!

111
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:30,997
- You’re not coming? - No.

112
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:44,135
[KARA BREATHING HEAVILY]

113
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:45,178
[JAO] Kara?

114
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:48,848
[RAPID FOOTSTEPS ON STAIRS]

115
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:59,609
[KARA CRYING SOFTLY]

116
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:10,952
[KARA CRYING SOFTLY]

117
00:06:10,953 --> 00:06:16,876
[KARA BREATHING HEAVILY]

118
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:18,669
So, that’s Jeremy?

119
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:23,091
Why is he here? Is he looking for me?

120
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,511
No.

121
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:30,556
He said he was surprised to see you here, too.

122
00:06:32,558 --> 00:06:33,559
Uh…

123
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:44,112
[KARA CRYING SOFTLY]

124
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,322
He said he wants to talk to you.

125
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:49,950
Just to see how you’re doing.

126
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,452
I don’t want to talk to him.

127
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:57,375
- Kara. - [KARA BREATHING HEAVILY]

128
00:06:59,127 --> 00:07:00,920
It’s been over seven years.

129
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:03,714
Why does...

130
00:07:03,756 --> 00:07:04,923
[KARA BREATHING HEAVILY]

131
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:07,927
Why does Jeremy still seem to have power over you?

132
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:12,806
[KARA BREATHING HEAVILY]

133
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,809
Jao’s outside waiting for you.

134
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:21,274
He wanted to know if you’re okay.

135
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:25,027
Do you want to talk to him?

136
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:29,407
Not yet, Carol. I just want to be alone.

137
00:07:33,995 --> 00:07:35,997
Want me to bring you a beer?

138
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:42,128
[KARA CRYING SOFTLY]

139
00:07:42,253 --> 00:07:43,462
Kara.

140
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,215
Caitlyn.

141
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:50,178
Whoever you may be...

142
00:07:52,054 --> 00:07:54,640
Kara deserves to be happy.

143
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:58,186
[KARA CRYING SOFTLY]

144
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:00,521
[CAROL] Caitlyn deserves...

145
00:08:01,063 --> 00:08:02,481
to be free.

146
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:07,111
[CAROL] Hm?

147
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:09,739
[KARA BREATHING HEAVILY]

148
00:08:13,492 --> 00:08:14,702
I'll get the beer.

149
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:26,756
[KARA BREATHING HEAVILY]

150
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:34,722
[KARA CRYING SOFTLY]

151
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,850
[FIRE CRACKLING]

152
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:52,967
You don’t have to say anything.

153
00:09:55,803 --> 00:09:57,805
I just want you to know that I’m here.

154
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:04,979
[KARA EXHALES]

155
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:09,734
I was still a kid when my parents split up.

156
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:17,867
Eventually, they both started new families.

157
00:10:20,077 --> 00:10:22,079
But neither of them wanted to take me in.

158
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:26,250
I ended up with my grandmother.

159
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:31,087
[KARA BREATHES DEEPLY]

160
00:10:31,088 --> 00:10:33,090
I felt so...

161
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:35,968
unwanted.

162
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:40,056
My grandmother loved me.

163
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:43,100
She gave me everything.

164
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,562
But something was missing.

165
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:51,233
So I kept looking for it in other people.

166
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:57,198
Until, eventually…

167
00:10:59,575 --> 00:11:01,077
I met Jeremy.

168
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,876
I was his executive assistant at his...

169
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:12,671
family’s steel and mining company.

170
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:15,383
And then...

171
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:17,760
that was it.

172
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:24,558
He made me feel like

173
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,602
I was his whole world.

174
00:11:31,857 --> 00:11:37,071
And for someone who felt so unwanted her whole life,

175
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:41,325
that meant everything.

176
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:52,002
His parents were kind to me, too.

177
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:52,878
[KARA SNIFFS]

178
00:11:52,879 --> 00:11:55,506
They really treated me like I was one of their own.

179
00:11:58,175 --> 00:12:00,678
I also felt so...

180
00:12:00,719 --> 00:12:01,846
needed.

181
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,433
I was so happy because I thought,

182
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:06,809
“Finally.”

183
00:12:09,895 --> 00:12:11,897
"Finally, I have a family."

184
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:12,940
[KARA SNIFFS]

185
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:16,902
All of that…

186
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:23,325
All of that became my life raft.

187
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:29,832
[KARA BREATHING SHAKILY]

188
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:32,084
And no matter what happened,

189
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:35,713
I will never let go of that raft.

190
00:12:35,754 --> 00:12:36,755
[KARA SNIFFS]

191
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:40,718
Even when Jeremy was already cheating on me.

192
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:45,389
[KARA SNIFFS AND BREATHES HEAVILY]

193
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:51,312
Where’s Ariel?

194
00:12:51,562 --> 00:12:52,770
Charging his phone.

195
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:56,066
Okay. Oh, it’s hot.

196
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:00,946
Mhmm! Sikwate! (Traditional Filipino hot chocolate drink)

197
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,155
Perfect for the vibes,

198
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:03,365
[SIARGAONON] for sure!

199
00:13:05,951 --> 00:13:07,453
[PEARL HUMMING]

200
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,462
Sir Han?

201
00:13:17,796 --> 00:13:19,798
Why is your face like that?

202
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:32,520
Pearl.

203
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:36,482
I want to tell you something.

204
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:42,111
Oh...

205
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:43,906
That sounds so serious.

206
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:47,326
I’m getting nervous.

207
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:48,994
Yeah.

208
00:13:49,453 --> 00:13:51,121
You should feel nervous.

209
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:53,457
Because…

210
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:00,214
Because…

211
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:03,592
the deadline for the application is due soon.

212
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:06,971
You really should start working on it.

213
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:10,349
Yes, Sir Han. Actually,

214
00:14:10,724 --> 00:14:12,518
with our talk earlier,

215
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:15,062
I’m now excited to do the essay.

216
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:18,023
I know. But please,

217
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:19,400
like I told you,

218
00:14:19,775 --> 00:14:22,486
write about you instead of me.

219
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:27,783
Don’t worry, Sir Han. I’ll take care of it.

220
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:33,414
Actually,

221
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:35,666
I have a question for you.

222
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:36,792
What?

223
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:40,713
Why are you so nice to me?

224
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:48,470
But I stayed.

225
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:53,058
I stayed.

226
00:14:56,061 --> 00:14:56,770
[KARA SNIFFS]

227
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:59,732
Even though he kept cheating on me.

228
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:03,193
I was just there.

229
00:15:06,196 --> 00:15:07,239
[KARA SNIFFS]

230
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:11,076
I even said yes when he asked me to marry him.

231
00:15:16,915 --> 00:15:19,792
[KARA SOBS]

232
00:15:19,793 --> 00:15:22,087
Because I thought I could fix it.

233
00:15:26,216 --> 00:15:28,385
I’d waited my whole life for something like that.

234
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:30,845
I finally got it.

235
00:15:30,846 --> 00:15:31,847
[KARA SNIFFS]

236
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:35,768
And I became terrified of losing it.

237
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,062
[KARA BREATHES SHAKILY]

238
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:45,110
I didn’t want to feel unloved again.

239
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:48,947
So, I did everything for them.

240
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:56,497
[KARA CRIES]

241
00:15:56,538 --> 00:15:59,041
I told you I love deeply.

242
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,003
No one’s judging you here.

243
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:07,633
What they did to me was awful.

244
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:13,639
[KARA BREATHES DEEPLY]

245
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:14,682
[KARA SCOFFS]

246
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:17,225
[KARA BREATHES SHAKILY]

247
00:16:17,226 --> 00:16:20,854
Until now, I still haven’t forgiven myself for it.

248
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:25,818
[KARA CRIES]

249
00:16:25,984 --> 00:16:29,488
I don’t know why I let that happen to me.

250
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:32,074
[KARA BREATHES SHAKILY]

251
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:37,246
Kara.

252
00:16:37,955 --> 00:16:39,164
[KARA BREATHES DEEPLY]

253
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:42,626
You have to give credit to yourself.

254
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,714
Because you walked out of that relationship.

255
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:52,094
It doesn’t matter how long it took you, you got out.

256
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:54,930
[KARA SNIFFS]

257
00:16:54,972 --> 00:16:56,974
You saved yourself.

258
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:00,561
[JAO] Don’t you realize?

259
00:17:02,938 --> 00:17:04,940
You were the life raft.

260
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:06,984
[KARA CRIES SOFTLY]

261
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:10,571
You saved yourself the moment you walked out of that relationship.

262
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:16,368
So stop punishing yourself.

263
00:17:16,952 --> 00:17:21,205
[KARA BREATHES SHAKILY]

264
00:17:21,206 --> 00:17:23,083
[JAO] I've made my share of...

265
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:27,171
questionable decisions, too.

266
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,466
Decisions that...

267
00:17:31,049 --> 00:17:32,885
challenged my beliefs.

268
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:37,139
But that’s life.

269
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:40,100
We’re only human.

270
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:45,439
So, please, Kara.

271
00:17:46,899 --> 00:17:48,901
You have to forgive yourself.

272
00:17:51,069 --> 00:17:53,071
Don’t feel guilty for wanting to be loved.

273
00:17:53,947 --> 00:17:55,449
Because you found it.

274
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:58,786
You found you.

275
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:03,207
You found it on this island.

276
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:06,502
[KARA BREATHES SHAKILY]

277
00:18:08,003 --> 00:18:10,172
You were broken and shattered into pieces,

278
00:18:10,297 --> 00:18:12,007
but look at you now.

279
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:17,638
Look at the life you’ve built here, the community you’ve fostered.

280
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:20,516
The influence that you have on me,

281
00:18:21,517 --> 00:18:24,603
on all of us on this island.

282
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:26,814
[KARA EXHALES]

283
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:31,944
You didn't just find yourself.

284
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:36,073
You reinvented yourself.

285
00:18:39,576 --> 00:18:42,162
If that isn’t self-love, then I don’t know what is.

286
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:51,088
I’m hard to love, Jao.

287
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:53,757
I’m ready to love you, Kara.

288
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:16,363
[JAO] Do you want to know what I told Ruth?

289
00:19:16,613 --> 00:19:18,740
[JAO] I'm ready to love you, Kara.

290
00:19:20,075 --> 00:19:22,411
Sir Han, why are you being so nice to me?

291
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:24,162
I think I forgot something.

292
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:26,081
- [HAN BIN CLEARS THROAT] - Sir Han!

293
00:19:26,456 --> 00:19:27,457
Okay.

294
00:19:29,084 --> 00:19:30,752
[HAN BIN SPEAKS KOREAN] The thing is…

295
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:33,338
[SIARGAONON] Are you planning to stay here, sir?

296
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,966
I think I might stay here for good.

297
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:37,717
There it is!

298
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:39,845
The curse got you, too!

299
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:41,846
I really fell hard for Kara.

300
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:43,557
[JEREMY] I just wanted to talk to you because...

301
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:45,267
I just wanted to check on you.

302
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:46,643
I was…

303
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:49,897
I was so afraid of you.

304
00:19:49,938 --> 00:19:51,607
[KARA] I was completely crushed.

305
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:55,485
[JEREMY] What’s going on? It’s been years, Caitlyn.

306
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:57,529
I thought that was in the past.
